      "title": "Mendel's Laws of Inheritance",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIa-b-1",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe Mendel's experiments.</li><li>State his three laws of inheritance.</li><li>Differentiate genotype from phenotype.</li><li>Define key genetic terms.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Allele</strong> — alternative form of a gene.</li><li><strong>Genotype</strong> — genetic makeup (e.g., Tt).</li><li><strong>Phenotype</strong> — observable trait (e.g., tall).</li><li><strong>Homozygous</strong> — two identical alleles.</li><li><strong>Heterozygous</strong> — two different alleles.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Mendel's Experiments</h4><p>Gregor Mendel (1860s) crossed pea plants to study inheritance. He tracked traits like flower color, seed shape, and plant height.</p><h4>B. Mendel's Laws</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Law</th><th>Statement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Law of Dominance</strong></td><td>One allele masks the other in heterozygotes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Law of Segregation</strong></td><td>Alleles separate during gamete formation</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Law of Independent Assortment</strong></td><td>Genes for different traits sort independently</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>C. Key Notation</h4><ul><li><strong>Dominant allele:</strong> uppercase (T)</li><li><strong>Recessive allele:</strong> lowercase (t)</li><li>Genotypes: TT, Tt, tt</li><li>Phenotypes: tall (TT, Tt), short (tt)</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "mendel-master",
        "badgeName": "Mendel Master",
        "badgeIcon": "🌱",
        "pairs": [
          { "key": "allele", "left": "Allele", "right": "Alternative form of a gene" },
          { "key": "geno", "left": "Genotype", "right": "Genetic makeup" },
          { "key": "pheno", "left": "Phenotype", "right": "Observable trait" },
          { "key": "homo", "left": "Homozygous", "right": "Two identical alleles" },
          { "key": "hetero", "left": "Heterozygous", "right": "Two different alleles" },
          { "key": "dom", "left": "Law of Dominance", "right": "One allele masks the other" },
          { "key": "seg", "left": "Law of Segregation", "right": "Alleles separate" }
        ]
      },
