      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Predict offspring genotypes with a Punnett square.</li><li>Calculate phenotypic and genotypic ratios.</li><li>Interpret monohybrid crosses.</li><li>Distinguish genotype from phenotype ratios.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Punnett square</strong> — grid showing possible offspring genotypes.</li><li><strong>Monohybrid cross</strong> — tracks one trait.</li><li><strong>Phenotypic ratio</strong> — ratio of visible traits.</li><li><strong>Genotypic ratio</strong> — ratio of genetic makeups.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Tt × Tt Cross</h4><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>T</th><th>t</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>T</strong></td><td>TT</td><td>Tt</td></tr><tr><td><strong>t</strong></td><td>Tt</td><td>tt</td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li>Genotypes: 1 TT : 2 Tt : 1 tt (1:2:1)</li><li>Phenotypes: 3 Tall : 1 Short</li></ul><h4>B. TT × tt Cross</h4><ul><li>All offspring: Tt (all tall)</li></ul><h4>C. Tt × tt (Testcross)</h4><ul><li>1 Tt : 1 tt → 1 tall : 1 short</li></ul>",
