      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Set up a dihybrid cross.</li><li>Predict offspring from two traits.</li><li>Identify the 9:3:3:1 ratio.</li><li>Apply the law of independent assortment.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Dihybrid cross</strong> — tracks two traits at once.</li><li><strong>Independent assortment</strong> — alleles for different genes sort independently.</li><li><strong>9:3:3:1</strong> — the classic dihybrid phenotypic ratio.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. RrYy × RrYy Cross</h4><p>R = round, r = wrinkled; Y = yellow, y = green.</p><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>RY</th><th>Ry</th><th>rY</th><th>ry</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>RY</strong></td><td>RRYY</td><td>RRYy</td><td>RrYY</td><td>RrYy</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Ry</strong></td><td>RRYy</td><td>RRyy</td><td>RrYy</td><td>Rryy</td></tr><tr><td><strong>rY</strong></td><td>RrYY</td><td>RrYy</td><td>rrYY</td><td>rrYy</td></tr><tr><td><strong>ry</strong></td><td>RrYy</td><td>Rryy</td><td>rrYy</td><td>rryy</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>B. Phenotypic Ratio</h4><ul><li><strong>9</strong> — Round, Yellow</li><li><strong>3</strong> — Round, Green</li><li><strong>3</strong> — Wrinkled, Yellow</li><li><strong>1</strong> — Wrinkled, Green</li></ul>",
