      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain the purpose of a testcross.</li><li>Determine unknown genotypes.</li><li>Interpret basic pedigree charts.</li><li>Trace inheritance through a family.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Testcross</strong> — crossing with a homozygous recessive to reveal genotype.</li><li><strong>Pedigree</strong> — diagram of inheritance in a family.</li><li><strong>Carrier</strong> — heterozygote that doesn't show the trait.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Testcross</h4><p>Cross an organism with dominant phenotype (but unknown genotype) with a homozygous recessive:</p><ul><li>If all offspring show dominant → parent was homozygous (TT)</li><li>If 1:1 ratio → parent was heterozygous (Tt)</li></ul><h4>B. Pedigree Symbols</h4><ul><li>□ Male · ○ Female · ■/● Affected</li><li>Horizontal line = mating</li><li>Vertical line = offspring</li></ul><h4>C. Reading a Pedigree</h4><ul><li>Track traits through generations</li><li>Identify carriers</li><li>Determine dominant vs recessive inheritance</li></ul>",
